      "rationale": "Directly categorizes the type of praise, which is exactly the axis the query needs for grouping and comparison. Mostly well-grounded, but row IMDB-0003 assigns 'acting_performance' as praise when the source calls the performances 'wooden' — a contradiction (that is a complaint, not praise), indicating some misattribution."
    },
    {
      "name": "complaint_type",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.95,
      "source_groundedness": 0.9,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Provides a genuine complaint-category axis central to the query. Sampled values are sound readings: insipid writing→screenplay_writing, terrible King movie→screenplay_writing, wooden/predictable premise→screenplay_writing. Silent rows correctly marked not_present."
    },
    {
      "name": "subject_target",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.82,
      "source_groundedness": 0.85,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a useful cross-cutting dimension (what the sentiment is about) enabling grouping beyond praise/complaint type. Mostly grounded, though IMDB-0004 tagged 'performance_actor' is a stretch when praise there centers on visuals/atmosphere and appearance rather than acting per se, but the text does mention acting so it is defensible."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.92,
  "source_groundedness": 0.82,
  "rationale": "All three columns give genuine, non-redundant analytical axes that directly serve the query about praise and complaints in IMDb reviews, supporting grouping and comparison. Grounding is generally sound with correct use of 'not_present' for silent rows, but there is at least one clear misattribution (praise_type on IMDB-0003 labeling 'wooden' performances as acting praise) and a borderline subject_target assignment, lowering groundedness modestly."
}

